<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 2.110 points off UK's FTSE index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 2.110 points off UK's FTSE index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International said the following FTSE-100 stocks will go ex-dividend on Monday and the effect will be to take 2.110 points off the index at the start of trading.</p>
<p>							DIVIDEND  INDEX</p>
<p>							(PENCE)   EFFECT</p>
<p>		 COMPANY			  Net	     Net</p>
<p>     * EMI Group plc			 22.00	    0.544</p>
<p>     * General Electric		     9.89	    1.565</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
